2, The summary of our invention
Our invention is designed to restore a low-quality facial image under extreme degradation conditions with high fidelity. Extreme degradation mainly refers to the severe loss of effective information in the portrait, such as in portraits taken with high magnification zoom, where information loss is caused by factors such as hardware limitations, object movement, or insufficient lighting. Diffusion techniques, as a general-purpose technology, are widely used in various visual tasks. However, when using diffusion techniques to improve extremely degraded facial images, two major issues arise: 1) the restored image lacks fidelity; 2) artifacts may be generated. Our invention aims to address these two major issues. Fig. 1 illustrates the main approach of our invention.
As shown in Fig. 1, to address the issue of lack of fidelity, our invention utilizes a high-quality reference facial image and introduces two components: the Efficient ID Extractor and the Texture Fidelity Preserver. These are specifically designed to ensure fidelity in terms of identity and texture, respectively. Additionally, an Adaptive Negative Reference Constructor is designed to guide the diffusion process to avoid generating artifacts.
 
Fig. 1 The solution of our invention
Specifically, our solution can be expanded as follows (as shown in Fig. 2). The high-distinguishability ID features extracted by the Efficient ID Extractor are applied during the diffusion process in the latent space, while the extracted texture features dynamically correct the intermediate diffusion results. Similarly, the constructed negative samples also influence the diffusion process in the latent space, guiding the diffusion model to avoid generating artifacts.
 
Fig.2 The detail of our invention

The main innovations of our invention：
1. Efficient ID Extractor 
Determine the neutral face image corresponding to the high-quality reference face image. Based on the neutral face image, separate the user's personalized features (such as moles, wrinkles, and scars) from the reference face image. Based on the 3D geometric consistency between the reference face image and the input face image, and the user's control input, determine the reference weights for the personalized features separated from the reference face image. Using these weights and the separated personalized features, obtain the personalized features needed to restore the input face image. (Fig. 3).
 
Fig. 3 The structure of Efficient ID Extractor
2. Texture Fidelity Preserver
Based on personalized features, after reconstructing the face image using the diffusion model, perform local corrections on the texture features of the reconstructed face image to ensure semantic consistency with the diffusion model's reconstruction, thereby further ensuring the consistency of texture features. (Fig. 4)
 
Fig. 4 Local texture corrections
3. Adaptive Negative Reference Constructor
Dynamically generate negative reference for the diffusion model based on different input image. By detecting the regions in the input image where characteristic artifacts may occur, generate semantically related artifact for these regions and degrade the generated distorted face to get negative reference for reconstructing the input image in a diffusion model. (Fig. 5)
 
